---
interface Props { kind: 'identity' | 'tenant' | 'range' | 'removal'; }
const {kind} = Astro.props;
const titles = {identity:'Three checks before a customer row returns',tenant:'The same query, a different trusted context',range:'Available is not fully protected',removal:'Finish each responsibility before retiring the store'};
const nums = {identity:1,tenant:2,range:3,removal:4};
---
<figure class="op-figure" data-operation-figure={kind} aria-label={titles[kind]}>
  <figcaption><span>Figure {nums[kind]}</span> {titles[kind]}</figcaption>
  <div class="op-scene">
    {kind === 'identity' && <>
      <div class="op-flow">
        <div class="op-box"><strong>Shop service</strong><p>Trusts cluster CA<br />Connects to <code>db.shop.example</code></p></div>
        <div class="op-arrow">⇄ <span>TLS connection</span></div>
        <div class="op-box"><strong>CockroachDB gateway</strong><p>Presents server certificate<br />Authenticates <code>shop_runtime</code></p></div>
      </div>
      <ol class="op-checks"><li><strong>Server identity</strong> The service checks the CA and requested hostname.</li><li><strong>SQL identity</strong> The gateway checks the runtime’s client certificate.</li><li><strong>Request authority</strong> The service checks the person; SQL privileges and a policy bound the database work.</li></ol>
      <p class="op-note">The person’s sign-in does not travel inside the SQL login. Tenant 10 is supplied separately, after the service authorises it.</p>
    </>}
    {kind === 'tenant' && <>
      <div class="op-options"><label>Tenant context <select data-tenant><option value="10">10 · authorised request</option><option value="20">20 · caller changes it</option><option value="">Missing</option></select></label></div>
      <p class="op-query"><code>SELECT customer_id, name FROM shop.customers;</code></p>
      <p class="op-stage">Stored customers → query result</p>
      <div class="op-rows" data-live>{[[1,10,'Mina Shah'],[2,10,'Tariq Aziz'],[3,10,'Edda Berg'],[4,20,'Rowan Vale']].map(([id,tenant,name])=><div class="op-row" data-row-tenant={tenant}><span>Tenant {tenant}</span><strong>{id} · {name}</strong><small data-row-state>Stored row</small></div>)}</div>
      <p class="op-result" data-live data-result>Result not yet returned.</p>
      <p class="op-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The runtime has SELECT authority. The query supplies no tenant condition.</p>
    </>}
    {kind === 'range' && <>
      <div class="op-options"><label>Another voter fails <select data-failure><option value="no">No</option><option value="yes">B also fails</option></select></label></div>
      <p class="op-stage" data-live data-stage>1. Three configured voters</p>
      <p class="op-note">One illustrative range · desired voters: 3 · majority: 2</p>
      <div class="op-nodes" data-live>{['A','B','C','D'].map(n=><div class="op-node" data-node={n}><strong>Node {n}</strong><span data-role>{n==='D'?'No replica':'Voter'}</span><small data-health>{n==='D'?'Eligible destination':'Reachable'}</small></div>)}</div>
      <div class="op-counts" data-live><p><strong data-count>3 / 3</strong><span>reachable voters</span></p><p><strong data-quorum>Present</strong><span>required majority</span></p><p><strong data-margin>One</strong><span>further voter failure tolerated</span></p></div>
      <p class="op-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">A, B and C hold the voting replicas. D has room for a replacement but supplies no vote.</p>
    </>}
    {kind === 'removal' && <>
      <ol class="op-removal"><li><strong>1 · Verify target and remaining cluster</strong><span>Node ID + address + cluster identity. Every affected range has a feasible placement and capacity budget.</span></li><li><strong>2 · Withdraw traffic and drain</strong><span>New requests use other gateways. Active SQL and serving roles leave. Stored replicas still exist.</span></li><li><strong>3 · Decommission the live target</strong><span>Normal pre-flight checks pass. Replicas move through supported membership changes.</span></li><li><strong>4 · Verify completion</strong><span>Membership is decommissioned; no target replicas remain; range protection and authorised service pass.</span></li><li><strong>5 · Stop the process and retire its store</strong><span>The planned unit is finished. Recheck health before starting another.</span></li></ol>
      <p class="op-note">A procedure model for permanent removal. A temporary stop drains and preserves the store for its return; it does not follow the permanent membership change.</p>
    </>}
  </div>
  {kind==='range' && <div class="op-controls" role="group" aria-label={`Figure ${nums[kind]} playback`}><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 4</span><div data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div></div>}
  <p class="op-caption">{kind==='identity'?'An illustrative secure self-hosted connection. The gateway may reach other nodes to obtain the requested rows; those internal requests are omitted.':kind==='tenant'?'A policy model over the four shared customer rows. Context is application_name, supplied by the service. The rows remain stored in every setting; the result changes.':kind==='range'?'Settled checkpoints for a fixed three-voter range and one replacement. Learner catch-up and the safe membership protocol are compressed between stages. These are quorum counts, not captured timing or live status metrics.':'Draining, evacuation and final membership answer different questions. A zero-replica progress row can precede final decommissioned membership.'}</p>
  {(kind==='tenant'||kind==='range') && <details><summary>Figure as text</summary>{kind==='tenant'?<p>The runtime can read the table. With context 10, customers 1–3 pass the policy and customer 4 does not. With context 20, only customer 4 passes. With no context, no row passes. The policy checks its supplied value, not whether the person was authorised to choose it.</p>:<p>Initially A, B and C vote. Losing C leaves A and B: a majority, with no further voter failure to spare. D receives a learner copy but cannot vote yet. After the supported replacement completes, A, B and D are the voters and one further voter can fail. If B is also unavailable before the replacement, only A remains from the old group: the planned replacement cannot simply be advanced by pressing Next.</p>}</details>}
</figure>

<script>
  import {stepper} from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-operation-figure]').forEach(root=>{
    const kind=root.dataset.operationFigure;
    if(kind!=='tenant'&&kind!=='range') return;
    const put=(selector:string,value:string)=>{const el=root.querySelector(selector);if(el)el.textContent=value;};
    if(kind==='tenant'){
      const drawTenant=()=>{
        const tenant=(root.querySelector('[data-tenant]') as HTMLSelectElement).value;
        let count=0;
        root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-row-tenant]').forEach(row=>{
          const pass=row.dataset.rowTenant===tenant;
          if(pass) count++;
          row.dataset.outcome=pass?'pass':'hidden';
          const el=row.querySelector('[data-row-state]'); if(el)el.textContent=pass?'Returned':'Not returned';
        });
        put('[data-result]',`${count} ${count===1?'row':'rows'} returned`);
        put('[data-explanation]',tenant==='20'?'The policy trusts this value. Changing it admits Rowan without checking the person’s right to choose tenant 20.':tenant==='10'?'The runtime can SELECT. The policy returns only rows matching context 10.':'No tenant ID matches the empty context, so the result is empty.');
      };
      root.querySelector('select')?.addEventListener('change',drawTenant);
      drawTenant();
      return;
    }
    const control=stepper(root,{steps:()=>4,draw:step=>{
      {
        const extra=(root.querySelector('[data-failure]') as HTMLSelectElement).value==='yes';
        const blocked=extra&&step>0;
        const final=step===3&&!blocked;
        put('[data-stage]',['1. Three configured voters','2. C is unreachable','3. D receives a learner copy',blocked?'4. Replacement blocked: old majority missing':'4. Replacement completed'][step]);
        root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-node]').forEach(node=>{
          const name=node.dataset.node;
          let role='Voter',health='Reachable',state='voter';
          if(name==='B'&&extra){health='Unreachable';state='down';}
          if(name==='C'&&step>0){health=final?'Removed from this range':'Unreachable';state='down';if(final)role='No longer a voter';}
          if(name==='D'){role=final?'Voter':step>=2?'Learner · no vote':'No replica';health=final?'Reachable':step>=2?'Receiving history':'Eligible destination';state=final?'voter':'learner';}
          node.dataset.state=state;node.querySelector('[data-role]')!.textContent=role;node.querySelector('[data-health]')!.textContent=health;
        });
        const count=step===0?(extra?2:3):final?3:extra?1:2;
        put('[data-count]',`${count} / 3`);put('[data-quorum]',count>=2?'Present':'Missing');put('[data-margin]',count===3?'One':count===2?'None':'Already unavailable');
        put('[data-explanation]',step===0?(extra?'B is unreachable. A and C still form a majority, but no further voter can fail.':'A, B and C hold the voting replicas. D has room for a replacement but supplies no vote.'):blocked?'A alone cannot form the old majority. A learner at D does not supply the missing vote. Restore a majority or use the documented recovery procedure; this model cannot advance the replacement.':step===1?'A and B still form two of the three votes. The range can progress, but losing either would remove its majority.':step===2?'D is receiving history as a learner. Until the safe membership change completes, the old voters still determine the majority.':'The completed voting set is A, B and D. Three reachable voters restore one further-voter-failure margin for this range.');
      }
    }});
    root.querySelector('select')?.addEventListener('change',()=>control.render());
  });
</script>

<style>
 .op-figure{margin:2.4rem 0;max-width:100%;font-family:var(--font-sans);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6}
 figcaption{margin-bottom:.65rem;font-family:var(--font-serif);font-size:1.15rem}figcaption>span{font: .7rem var(--font-mono);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.5rem}
 .op-scene{border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);padding:1.15rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt)}
 .op-flow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr .6fr 1fr;align-items:center;gap:.5rem}.op-box,.op-node{padding:.85rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface)}
 .op-box p{font: .83rem/1.65 var(--font-sans);margin:.6rem 0 0}.op-arrow{text-align:center;font-size:1.4rem;color:var(--color-text)}.op-arrow span{display:block;font-size:.7rem}
 .op-checks,.op-removal{padding-left:1.3rem;margin:1rem 0}.op-checks li{margin:.7rem 0}.op-checks strong{display:block}.op-note{font:.78rem/1.6 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin:.9rem 0 0}
 .op-options{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem;margin:0 0 1rem}.op-options label{font:.8rem var(--font-sans)}select{display:block;margin-top:.4rem;max-width:100%;padding:.5rem;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);border-radius:3px;font:inherit}
 .op-query{font:.75rem/1.6 var(--font-mono);padding:.7rem;border-left:3px solid var(--teal);overflow-wrap:anywhere}.op-stage{font-weight:600;margin:1rem 0}.op-rows{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.5rem}.op-row{padding:.7rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface)}.op-row span,.op-row strong,.op-row small{display:block}.op-row span,.op-row small{font-size:.75rem}.op-row[data-outcome=pass]{border:2px solid var(--teal);padding:calc(.7rem - 1px)}.op-row[data-outcome=hidden]{border-style:dashed}.op-row[data-outcome=hidden] strong{text-decoration:line-through}.op-result{font-size:.85rem;margin:.8rem 0 0}[data-operation-figure=tenant] .op-explanation{min-height:0}
 .op-explanation{border-left:3px solid var(--teal);padding:.2rem 0 .2rem .8rem;min-height:4.9rem;font:.86rem/1.7 var(--font-sans);margin:1rem 0 0}.op-controls{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.45rem;padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);border-top:0;background:var(--color-surface)}button{font: .78rem var(--font-sans);padding:.5rem .7rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);border-radius:4px;background:var(--color-surface-alt);color:var(--color-text);cursor:pointer}button[aria-disabled=true]{color:var(--color-text-secondary)}button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--teal);outline-offset:3px}[data-step]{font:.72rem var(--font-mono);margin-left:auto}[data-hold]{width:100%;height:2px;background:var(--color-rule)}[data-hold] span{display:block;width:0;height:2px;background:var(--teal)}
 .op-caption{font:.78rem/1.65 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin:.7rem 0}.op-figure details{font:.8rem/1.7 var(--font-sans)}.op-figure details p{font:inherit}.op-figure summary{cursor:pointer}
 .op-nodes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.5rem}.op-node strong,.op-node span,.op-node small{display:block}.op-node strong{font-size:.9rem}.op-node span{font-size:.8rem;margin:.5rem 0}.op-node small{font-size:.72rem}.op-node[data-state=voter]{border:2px solid var(--teal);padding:calc(.85rem - 1px)}.op-node[data-state=down]{border-style:dashed}.op-node[data-state=down] strong{text-decoration:line-through}.op-counts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule);gap:.6rem;margin-top:1rem}.op-counts p{font:.8rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);margin:1rem 0 0}.op-counts strong{font-size:1.15rem;display:block}.op-counts span{font-size:.73rem;display:block}
 .op-removal li{padding:0 0 1rem .5rem;border-left:2px solid var(--teal);list-style:none}.op-removal li:last-child{padding-bottom:0}.op-removal strong,.op-removal span{display:block}.op-removal span{font-size:.82rem;margin-top:.3rem}.op-removal{padding-left:0;margin:0}
 @media(max-width:550px){.op-scene{padding:.8rem}.op-flow{grid-template-columns:1fr}.op-arrow{padding:.3rem}.op-nodes{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.op-rows{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.op-row{padding:.5rem}.op-row[data-outcome=pass]{padding:calc(.5rem - 1px)}.op-explanation{min-height:7rem}.op-counts strong{font-size:1rem}.op-counts{gap:.4rem}.op-box{padding:.7rem}}
</style>
